      "error": {
        "code": 400,
        "message": "The non-transactional DML operation was rejected because it was impossible to guarantee document-level atomicity.\n\nFirestore guarantees that all non-transactional writes to a document are applied atomically by requiring that all field transforms (e.g. add_fields(...)) & filters (e.g. where(...)) reference only a single document at a time. For example the following is supported outside of a transaction:\n\n  collection_group('users')\n    | where(x = 1)\n    | where(y != 2)\n    | add_fields(add(z, 1) as z)\n    | update(add(a, 1) as a)\n\nEven though there are multiple different field transformations and filters, they all can be applied to a single document at one time. Conversely, DML operations that have preconditions across multiple documents cannot be supported outside of a transaction while ensuring this document-level atomicity. The most common way this happens is when attempting to perform an aggregation, unnest, union, search, or subquery as part of the non-transactional DML operation.\n\nTo work around this, either refactor the DML operation to not require these stages, perform the entire DML operation within a transaction, or use the 'atomic' setting provided by the SDKs.",
        "status": "INVALID_ARGUMENT",
        "details": [
          {
